properties":{"name":"Baratoria","kind":"island","rank":2,"source":"baratoria"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-5.98353,5.30043]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Grand Isle","kind":"island","rank":3,"source":"baratoria"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-5.98933,5.30017]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Walkers Cay","kind":"island","rank":3,"source":"baratoria"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-5.98345,5.3067]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"South Cay","kind":"island","rank":3,"source":"baratoria"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-5.98181,5.29554]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"The Steaming Peaks","kind":"mountain","rank":3,"source":"enaria"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-0.63825,6.90557]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"The Arctic Pole","kind":"region","rank":1,"source":"adjust","note":"Map distortion: a flat map cannot show a pole without stretching it, so the whole top of the map is the polar ice, smeared from edge to edge (and cut off here). The northern continent widens because it joins it. Distances this far north are not to scale."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-2.1875,11.13281]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"The Antarctic Pole","kind":"region","rank":1,"source":"adjust","note":"Map distortion again: the whole bottom of the map is the southern polar ice, smeared from edge to edge (and cut off here). It is smaller than the arctic cap, and its coast reaches out in long curving peninsulas. Distances this far south are not to scale."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-2.1875,-15.68359]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Volcanic Mountains","kind":"mountain","rank":3,"source":"adjust","note":"The volcanic mountains in whose crook Valkith lies; their cliffs fall to the Inner Sea in the north."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-6.91406,4.53125]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Peregrine's Islet","kind":"island","rank":3,"source":"adjust","note":"Called Peregrin's Table in the campaign, after the flat Sahuagin altar on its western hill (Mandiant's charts call it a small jut of rock covered in sea-bird droppings). Jungle covers its middle, with highlands, dunes and a marsh, and rivers running to the coast. Two small sandy islets lie to the north-east."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-11.05469,4.45313]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Skellig Rath","kind":"island","rank":3,"source":"adjust","note":"A bleak spire of rock in an angry sea, about a day's sail from Aillfar. Lair of the formorian Elgol."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-8.32031,3.39844]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Umbral Isle","kind":"island","rank":3,"source":"adjust","note":"A lonely island of lingering shadow, about three days' sailing north-west of Agrea. No animals or people live here. A cave guarded by two bronze dragon statues leads to The Three, who ask each visitor a truth in exchange for passage into Shadow."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-16.2207,1.23437]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Akanos Crater","kind":"region","rank":3,"source":"adjust","note":"Where the floating island Akanos was torn from the earth. About a fifth of the city of Atma, a round section of its north-eastern quarter, was lifted away and left this crater. Akanos does not stay anywhere: it drifts about the world, so it has no fixed place on this map."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-1.64453,4.09375]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Enaria","kind":"region","rank":2,"source":"adjust","note":"The elves' lost first home. Elven civilisation first rose here to great heights, until their experiments in high magic and time magic broke the land apart; it was lost in a great maelstrom of time energy, displaced in time and unreachable. The elves who fled came to the shores of Tel-Tenauril, but not all from the same Enaria: first the high elves, soon after the silver (moon) elves from another timeline, then over the next century or so more kinds of elf, each from a different lost Enaria, a result of the temporal storms. The daughter of the high mage who sundered Enaria, the chronomancer, has worked across many campaigns to change the timeline in small ways, so that she can attempt a great spell to steady Enaria and bring it back to the world. Its place on this map is a guess (the author: somewhere over the sea west or east of Tel-Tenauril), and its coasts, ranges and rivers are only one invented version: each timeline's Enaria differed."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-0.625,6.89453]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Border Mountains","kind":"mountain","rank":2,"source":"adjust"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-8.19336,4.80469]}}]}